nginx.conf is mounted at /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf → included in http context, so `limit_req_zone` at the top of the file (before server{}) is valid.

Routes: auth = `/auth/*`, upload = `POST /api/videos` (router prefix /api/videos, POST ""). Feed router = /api (feed, search).

nginx.conf C5 version:

```nginx
# ... header comment ...
# C5: IP-level rate limiting for the auth endpoints (the app layers its
# own per-account limits on top; this is the nginx perimeter).
limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=auth_per_ip:10m rate=10r/m;

server {
    listen 80;

    # Default body cap for everything; only the upload location overrides it.
    client_max_body_size 10m;

    # C5: baseline security headers on every response.
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff always;
    add_header X-Frame-Options DENY always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy no-referrer-when-downgrade always;

    # C5: auth endpoints are rate-limited at the proxy too (register/login
    # are the expensive ones: bcrypt cost 12).
    location /auth/ {
        limit_req zone=auth_per_ip burst=20 nodelay;
        proxy_pass http://web:8000;
        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }

    # C5: the ONLY place a 512m body is accepted is the upload endpoint;
    # streaming is unbuffered so the app can abort early on size.
    location = /api/videos {
        client_max_body_size 512m;
        proxy_request_buffering off;
        proxy_pass http://web:8000;
        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }

    location /videos/ { ... unchanged ... }
    location /thumbnails/ { ... }
    location /media/thumbnails/ { ... }

    location / {
        ... unchanged ...
    }
}
```

Wait: `location = /api/videos` matches only exact path — POST /api/videos (no trailing slash). Good. But also GET /api/videos? There's no such route (feed is /api/feed). Fine — but the exact-match location also captures any method to that path; acceptable.

Hmm, one issue: `location /auth/` prefix matches /auth/login, /auth/register, /auth/logout, /auth/me. limit_req burst=20 nodelay rate 10r/m — reasonable.

Also add_header with `always` in server context: nginx inheritance — add_header directives are inherited from server ONLY if the location has no add_header of its own. None of the locations add headers, so server-level applies everywhere. Good.

App-side upload: add request param + Content-Length pre-check in upload_video.

Tests:
- tests/test_nginx_config.py with a small block extractor.
- tests/test_review_c5_upload.py direct-call tests for the pre-check.

Write red tests first, run red, then apply nginx + app changes.

For the nginx test, helper to extract a block by prefix:

```python
def _block(text, start_marker):
    i = text.index(start_marker)
    j = text.index("{", i)
    depth = 0
    for k in range(j, len(text)):
        if text[k] == "{": depth += 1
        elif text[k] == "}":
