T7 done: 290 passed. Now T5 + T8 (nginx). Red test file tests/test_nginx_media_delivery.py:

T5 assertions:
- location /videos/ block: proxy_buffering off, proxy_max_temp_file_size 0 (no spool), proxy_request_buffering off (already), does NOT contain proxy_hide_header Content-Type / Content-Disposition, does not set proxy_set_header Range to something empty; ensure Range passthrough: nginx passes client headers by default; assert no `proxy_set_header Range` override... but explicit is better: add `proxy_set_header Range $http_range;`? Default already passes Range. Hmm — to make the test meaningful, assert that the block does NOT hide Range/Accept-Ranges/Content-Type/Content-Disposition (no proxy_hide_header for them) and proxy_buffering off + proxy_max_temp_file_size 0.
- /thumbnails/ and /media/thumbnails/ similar (buffering off optional for images but fine).

T8 assertions:
- every silo-proxying location (/videos/, /thumbnails/, /media/thumbnails/) contains proxy_hide_header X-Content-Type-Options (so upstream's nosniff doesn't duplicate nginx's add_header).
- /media/thumbnails/ (public thumbs) declares add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=3600" AND re-declares the 3 security headers (because add_header in a location cancels server-level inheritance).
- no location sets add_header Content-Type or add_header X-Frame-Options that would break <video>... X-Frame-Options doesn't affect <video>. Assert server-level add_header X-Frame-Options DENY present and media locations don't set frame-ancestors/CSP. Keep simple: assert X-Frame-Options present at server, and no `add_header Content-Disposition` anywhere, and no `proxy_hide_header Content-Type`.
- Cache-Control: videos are private/presigned → no long cache; assert /videos/ does NOT add Cache-Control public long max-age (privacy). Thumbnails public → max-age=3600.

Red now: current nginx.conf lacks proxy_buffering off in /videos/, lacks proxy_max_temp_file_size, lacks proxy_hide_header, lacks Cache-Control in /media/thumbnails/ → red.

Fix nginx.conf:

```
    location /videos/ {
        proxy_pass http://silo:9000;
        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
        # Stream video: never buffer the whole object to disk (Range/206 must work).
        proxy_request_buffering off;
        proxy_buffering off;
        proxy_max_temp_file_size 0;
        # Silo may send its own nosniff; hide it so nginx's server-level
        # add_header is the only one (no duplicate X-Content-Type-Options).
        proxy_hide_header X-Content-Type-Options;
    }

    location /thumbnails/ {
        proxy_pass http://silo:9000;
        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
        proxy_buffering off;
        proxy_max_temp_file_size 0;
        proxy_hide_header X-Content-Type-Options;
    }

    location /media/thumbnails/ {
        # Public-read bucket: rewrite /media/thumbnails/<obj> -> /thumbnails/<obj>
        rewrite ^/media/thumbnails/(.*)$ /thumbnails/$1 break;
        proxy_pass http://silo:9000;
        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
        proxy_buffering off;
        proxy_max_temp_file_size 0;
        # hide upstream nosniff — this location declares its own add_header
        # (Cache-Control), which cancels server-level add_header inheritance,
        # so the security headers are re-declared here explicitly.
        proxy_hide_header X-Content-Type-Options;
        add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff always;
        add_header X-Frame-Options DENY always;
        add_header Referrer-Policy no-referrer-when-downgrade always;
        # Public thumbnails are immutable per video id: cache 1h.
        add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=3600" always;
    }
```

Also update server-level comment line 23-24 ("none of them declare their own add_header" → now /media/thumbnails/ does, re-declaring them).

Note: proxy_hide_header X-Content-Type-Options in /videos/ and /thumbnails/ — those locations have no add_header, so server-level add_header applies → exactly one nosniff. Good.

Wait — does silo actually send X-Content-Type-Options? Owner observed duplicate, so yes.

Also item 5 mentions "должен пропускать заголовок Range и Accept-Ranges" — nginx passes Range to upstream by default (it's a client header, forwarded unless overridden) and Accept-Ranges from upstream is passed by default. To be explicit and test-friendly, add `proxy_set_header Range $http_range;`? That's the default behavior anyway (nginx passes $http_range as Range by default? Actually nginx by default passes the Range header unchanged; proxy_set_header Range $http_range is a no-op explicit). And `proxy_pass_header Accept-Ranges;` — Accept-Ranges is not in nginx's default hidden list, so it passes by default; proxy_pass_header makes it explicit. I'll add both lines with comments for clarity and test them.

Hmm, careful: `proxy_set_header Range $http_range;` — if client sends no Range, $http_range is empty → nginx does NOT send the header when value is empty (proxy_set_header with empty value = header not passed). Good.

Now the existing test test_silo_locations_keep_host_and_buffering expects proxy_request_buffering off in /videos/ — keep that line. It checks thumbs block has Host — keep.

Write red test file now.

